---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "Do I need an NVIDIA GPU for Mockingbird?",
    a: "No. The app runs on CPU, but an NVIDIA GPU with CUDA significantly speeds up speech recognition and cuts answer latency to ~2–5 seconds.",
  },
  {
    q: "Does my data go to the cloud?",
    a: "Only the LLM request leaves your machine. Speech recognition, the PDF résumé and the knowledge base are processed locally on your computer.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is Invisible Mode?",
    a: "A privacy mode in which the Mockingbird window is excluded from screen capture: during screen sharing and streaming it is invisible both in recordings and to viewers.",
  },
  {
    q: "Which platforms are supported?",
    a: "Windows 10/11 and Linux (x86_64).",
  },
  {
    q: "How much does Mockingbird cost?",
    a: "Free. The app is open source and available for download on the releases page.",
  },
  {
    q: "How fast is the answer?",
    a: "Typical latency is 2–5 seconds from the end of the question to the start of the answer on a GPU with CUDA. On CPU it takes longer.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I choose a speech recognition model?",
    a: "The default is faster-whisper large-v3-turbo — the best balance of accuracy and speed on GPU. On weaker hardware pick smaller models from the table in the 'Choosing an STT model' section.",
  },
];

const faqLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faq.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<DocsLayout
  title="FAQ"
  description="Common questions about Mockingbird: privacy, CUDA, Invisible Mode, price and supported platforms."
  jsonLd={faqLd}
  locale="en"
>
  <h1>FAQ</h1>
  <p>
    Answers to common questions about the Mockingbird technical interview assistant:
    privacy, hardware requirements, Invisible Mode and more.
  </p>

  <h2>Do I need an NVIDIA GPU?</h2>
  <p>
    No. On CPU recognition works, but slower. A GPU with CUDA accelerates
    <code>faster-whisper</code> and reduces answer latency.
  </p>

  <h2>Does my data go to the cloud?</h2>
  <p>
    Only the LLM request leaves your machine. Speech recognition, your résumé and
    the knowledge base are processed locally on your computer.
  </p>

  <h2>What is Invisible Mode?</h2>
  <p>
    The assistant window is excluded from screen capture: during sharing and
    streaming it is invisible both in recordings and to viewers.
  </p>

  <h2>Which platforms are supported?</h2>
  <p>Windows 10/11 and Linux (x86_64).</p>

  <h2>How much does Mockingbird cost?</h2>
  <p>Free, the source code is open.</p>

  <h2>The app doesn't see my GPU</h2>
  <p>
    Check your CUDA drivers and that the build ships with GPU support. The toolbar
    indicator should show <code>GPU</code>; otherwise <code>CPU</code> is used.
  </p>

  <h2>The answer takes too long</h2>
  <p>
    Typical latency is <strong>2–5 s</strong> from the end of the question to the
    answer on GPU. If it's longer — make sure the model is loaded and the GPU is active.
  </p>

  <h2>How do I update?</h2>
  <p>
    Via the <a href="https://github.com/Mockingbird-go-on/mockingbird/releases" target="_blank" rel="noopener">releases page</a>
    or through the new-version notification on startup.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
